		{"id":"02634d8373b60c29","type":"text","text":"**Initialization context**\n* Unity calls this at the “birth” of every particle, This defines the initial state of the particle.","x":-11780,"y":6891,"width":250,"height":274,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"956fdfabf6fef8d0","type":"text","text":"**Update context**\n* Unity calls this every frame for all particles, and uses this to perform simulations, for example Forces and Collisions.","x":-11780,"y":7243,"width":250,"height":320,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"394afbf168fc664d","type":"text","text":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/ParticleSystems.html","x":-14248,"y":7403,"width":612,"height":60},
		{"id":"e108077cd7521ba1","type":"text","text":"Size","x":-12660,"y":7403,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d00762c28927c3da","type":"text","text":"**Output context:**\n* Unity calls this every frame for every particle. This determines the shape of a particle, and performs pre-render transformations","x":-11780,"y":7677,"width":250,"height":284,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"3b91d82f4ac7f229","type":"text","text":"Unity Particle Systems","x":-14067,"y":6779,"width":250,"height":60},
