		{"id":"3ea9390e8fe96b80","type":"text","text":"Tangents on surface geometry","x":-5232,"y":4190,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2521614d04388988","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/InitialGeometry.jpg","x":-5867,"y":4449,"width":400,"height":233},
		{"id":"97877b403da123ca","type":"text","text":"Volume as datas tructure for storing vector field for particles: rasterize volume of surface containing vector field and volume advect in POP for particle simulation\n\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0SDptfygg\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yqM_3goH4J8\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rn_8iN7lyjI\n","x":-5807,"y":3449,"width":700,"height":280},
		{"id":"fe39c43c86829a69","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/InitialGeometryTangents.jpg","x":-5317,"y":4441,"width":400,"height":250},
		{"id":"6d52b6b5da9319e8","type":"text","text":"Advection:\n\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advection\n* In the fields of [physics](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physics \"Physics\"), [engineering](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Engineering \"Engineering\"), and [earth sciences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth_science \"Earth science\"), **advection** is the [transport](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transport \"Transport\") of a substance or quantity by bulk motion of a fluid.\n* During advection, a fluid transports some conserved quantity or material via bulk motion. The fluid's motion is described [mathematically](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics \"Mathematics\") as a [vector field](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vector_field \"Vector field\"), and the transported material is described by a [scalar field](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scalar_field \"Scalar field\") showing its distribution over space.","x":-5037,"y":3449,"width":710,"height":280},
		{"id":"9737fbea700a8ddc","type":"text","text":"Useful for:\n* Custom vector fields\n* Phenomenological fluid simulation\n\t* https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterize.html","x":-3397,"y":4301,"width":380,"height":204},
		{"id":"e105bd1efe59fb2c","type":"text","text":"Particle-based fluid simulation approaches:\n* SPH \n* PSD\n* FLIP\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bx_D_51bF7Y","x":-2094,"y":4475,"width":724,"height":200},
		{"id":"fd28dc3ba65d4eac","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K0cNvpXujmk","x":-2838,"y":4499,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"5f3cb7798841531e","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/VolumeRasterizeAttributes.jpg","x":-3417,"y":4627,"width":400,"height":239},
		{"id":"b78dada2ae1751fc","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rC9EGQJOLyE","x":-2839,"y":3650,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"a17a57a394b8d1e7","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WKDY5b_V5go","x":-2839,"y":4075,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"f314603fa2f70dbf","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JS3rw7W1gN4","x":-2838,"y":3220,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"59c875b8e9ed0a64","type":"text","text":"**Procedural modeling** of phenomenological fuzzy objects: \n* particle advection by volume vector field\n\nExample:\n1. Mesh is used to generate main shape (only surface).\n2. Differential geometry OPs are used to compute information per surface points (e.g., tangent field)\n3. Surface is rasterized into volume grid where each cell is assigned with vector value\n4. Particle simulation is using volume grid information for movement.\n\nExample:\n1. Mesh is used to generate main shape (only surface).\n2. Mesh is rasterized: converted to grid\n3. Noise is computed for each grid cell resulting in volume vector field\n4. Particle simulation is using volume grid information for movement.","x":-2094,"y":3538,"width":620,"height":502},
		{"id":"710fa593121a4305","type":"text","text":"Point Cloud Open and Point Cloud Filter VOP/VEX nodes/functions are used to access point information around current particle in POP VOP. This way, vector field stored at points can be used to drive particles.\n\nIt can be used for any kind of points in surface or volume:\n1. Surface points: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zJls__AJlJo\n2. Volume points: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JS3rw7W1gN4&t=11s ","x":-2094,"y":4121,"width":724,"height":314},
		{"id":"7297572f0989bdd3","type":"text","text":"VDB Density","x":-3911,"y":6065,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f2e5a1cd8479652c","type":"text","text":"ParticlesVolumeAdvection Example. TODO rename!","x":-3831,"y":6904,"width":571,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3c26ac655ad6270f","type":"text","text":"Convert particles to volume and rendering:\n* https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/42457/\n* Volume rasterize particles: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterizeparticles.html\n* Volume rasterize points: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterizepoints.html\n* Volume rasterize attributes: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterizeattributes.html + https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0SDptfygg\n* Volume color: https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/53590/?page=1#post-351635 + https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/paintcolorvolume.html","x":-3765,"y":7334,"width":700,"height":367},
